[{:db/id "5c780ba2-f667-560d-b8e1-248ea20cfe21" :answer/id #uuid "5c780ba2-f667-560d-b8e1-248ea20cfe21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "441faa0c-6a70-5ffa-a2f7-be85bc15c8e6" :answer/id #uuid "441faa0c-6a70-5ffa-a2f7-be85bc15c8e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f26d4ab5-5aed-5a95-963f-4870415729d0" :answer/id #uuid "f26d4ab5-5aed-5a95-963f-4870415729d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "60d8a298-d4e4-570a-a583-6f173784c347" :answer/id #uuid "60d8a298-d4e4-570a-a583-6f173784c347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f54f3396-5ed6-5d96-b187-6458849c0b77" :answer/id #uuid "f54f3396-5ed6-5d96-b187-6458849c0b77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c986d9b3-6cbe-5371-bfa3-6e711d83e7d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "c986d9b3-6cbe-5371-bfa3-6e711d83e7d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["5c780ba2-f667-560d-b8e1-248ea20cfe21" "441faa0c-6a70-5ffa-a2f7-be85bc15c8e6" "f26d4ab5-5aed-5a95-963f-4870415729d0" "60d8a298-d4e4-570a-a583-6f173784c347" "f54f3396-5ed6-5d96-b187-6458849c0b77"] :answer-field/correct "5c780ba2-f667-560d-b8e1-248ea20cfe21" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "80d403dd-76fc-5ee3-bdb6-3cb3268156ab" :question/id #uuid "80d403dd-76fc-5ee3-bdb6-3cb3268156ab" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):0\\le x\\le 6,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 2\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n0\\le x\\le 6,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 2,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x + y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 6,\\,0\\le v\\le 2\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=1=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- u + v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta v\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(v\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} [\\int_{0}^{6} v\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v[\\int_{0}^{6} 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v\\left[u\\right]_{0}^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v\\left(\\left(6\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(6\\right)\\int_{0}^{2} v\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(6\\right)\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(6\\right)\\left(\\left(2\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(6\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["c986d9b3-6cbe-5371-bfa3-6e711d83e7d3"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d1356060-39d5-5aaa-b169-5db31bf6e216" :answer/id #uuid "d1356060-39d5-5aaa-b169-5db31bf6e216" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c82d237b-949e-5412-9a23-644f15704339" :answer/id #uuid "c82d237b-949e-5412-9a23-644f15704339" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4e765720-8714-5718-9764-131162472f11" :answer/id #uuid "4e765720-8714-5718-9764-131162472f11" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a64880cd-bff1-5620-b356-4231dbbdc31f" :answer/id #uuid "a64880cd-bff1-5620-b356-4231dbbdc31f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8e1d840f-cd7a-554f-a993-fb34c29588fe" :answer/id #uuid "8e1d840f-cd7a-554f-a993-fb34c29588fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "48ef6c02-8c42-5abc-b344-f7059a