 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=1=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- u + v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta v\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(v\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} [\\int_{0}^{4} v\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v[\\int_{0}^{4} 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v\\left[u\\right]_{0}^{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{2} v\\left(\\left(4\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(4\\right)\\int_{0}^{2} v\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(4\\right)\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{2} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(4\\right)\\left(\\left(2\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(4\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right) \\\\ & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["48ef6c02-8c42-5abc-b344-f7059ae6a63e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "bdaf610d-9c5e-5495-9e74-f6cc3d09e83d" :answer/id #uuid "bdaf610d-9c5e-5495-9e74-f6cc3d09e83d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{21}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1adc1044-a21c-5fb5-a7dd-710c0183e0a6" :answer/id #uuid "1adc1044-a21c-5fb5-a7dd-710c0183e0a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{63}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "88d08105-5bc0-5b01-aba1-ad81db0f73d2" :answer/id #uuid "88d08105-5bc0-5b01-aba1-ad81db0f73d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{63}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "730e8a89-1885-53bc-968e-db1e396f42e2" :answer/id #uuid "730e8a89-1885-53bc-968e-db1e396f42e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ce359bd0-213f-5208-b73b-97a593b89e7b" :answer/id #uuid "ce359bd0-213f-5208-b73b-97a593b89e7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "63" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "94a3a1f5-e60e-5c3b-8422-1ee5205aa1f0" :answer-field/id #uuid "94a3a1f5-e60e-5c3b-8422-1ee5205aa1f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["bdaf610d-9c5e-5495-9e74-f6cc3d09e83d" "1adc1044-a21c-5fb5-a7dd-710c0183e0a6" "88d08105-5bc0-5b01-aba1-ad81db0f73d2" "730e8a89-1885-53bc-968e-db1e396f42e2" "ce359bd0-213f-5208-b73b-97a593b89e7b"] :answer-field/correct "1adc1044-a21c-5fb5-a7dd-710c0183e0a6" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "4f71a0e9-4f26-53c3-82c6-851fe7d02505" :question/id #uuid "4f71a0e9-4f26-53c3-82c6-851fe7d02505" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):0\\le x\\le 7,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n0\\le x\\le 7,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x + y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 7,\\,0\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=1=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- u + v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta v\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(v\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{3} [\\int_{0}^{7} v\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{3} v[\\int_{0}^{7} 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{3} v\\left[u\\right]_{0}^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{3} v\\left(\\left(7\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\int_{0}^{3} v\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{3} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{63}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["94a3a1f5-e60e-5c3b-8422-1ee5205aa1f0"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d0ab8ec1-ca97-5fc9-a9d7-cc00f8c41967" :answer/id #uuid "d0ab8ec1-ca97-5fc9-a9d7-cc00f8c41967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "18" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "667a6e43-b6f9-5aa8-9c14-d1fe22bd70fc" :answer/id #uuid "667a6e43-b6f9-5aa8-9c14-d1fe22bd70fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "281e4fec-c587-55e5-9466-7d86996844e1" :answer/id #uuid "281e4fec-c587-55e5-9466-7d86996844e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "72" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "57377b59-9410-5e89-b4f8-e9b944c753b4" :answer/id #uuid "57377b59-9410-5e89-b4f8-e9b944c753b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2a1950a3-40b6-5898-b425-c531