Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le 6\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=1=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- u + v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta v\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(v\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{6} [\\int_{0}^{2} v\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{6} v[\\int_{0}^{2} 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{6} v\\left[u\\right]_{0}^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{6} v\\left(\\left(2\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right)\\int_{0}^{6} v\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right)\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{6} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right)\\left(\\left(18\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(18\\right) \\\\ & =36\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["043c8455-12eb-5905-ac4f-cc892ffbc581"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d0e0f8f1-6ea0-513a-b3ba-c5a3e3006fde" :answer/id #uuid "d0e0f8f1-6ea0-513a-b3ba-c5a3e3006fde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "175" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6371b1f1-1af0-5676-a83f-e3af25e85ecf" :answer/id #uuid "6371b1f1-1af0-5676-a83f-e3af25e85ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{175}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ae6822e3-2e4c-5b8e-bf92-73cb98cf24fd" :answer/id #uuid "ae6822e3-2e4c-5b8e-bf92-73cb98cf24fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{175}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "2e977e94-e980-530b-8907-438b199a2f50" :answer/id #uuid "2e977e94-e980-530b-8907-438b199a2f50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{35}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a788eda2-0113-57f1-b04a-35460668f9fe" :answer/id #uuid "a788eda2-0113-57f1-b04a-35460668f9fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ecfa51a6-08a6-519a-a1b0-6bb584bc2c63" :answer-field/id #uuid "ecfa51a6-08a6-519a-a1b0-6bb584bc2c63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d0e0f8f1-6ea0-513a-b3ba-c5a3e3006fde" "6371b1f1-1af0-5676-a83f-e3af25e85ecf" "ae6822e3-2e4c-5b8e-bf92-73cb98cf24fd" "2e977e94-e980-530b-8907-438b199a2f50" "a788eda2-0113-57f1-b04a-35460668f9fe"] :answer-field/correct "6371b1f1-1af0-5676-a83f-e3af25e85ecf" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "f3bd7c92-8f56-539e-bf05-cdd21947011e" :question/id #uuid "f3bd7c92-8f56-539e-bf05-cdd21947011e" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):0\\le x\\le 7,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 5\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n0\\le x\\le 7,\\quad 0\\le x + y\\le 5,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x + y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):0\\le u\\le 7,\\,0\\le v\\le 5\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=1=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- u + v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x + y\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta v\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(v\\right)\\cdot \\left(1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{5} [\\int_{0}^{7} v\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{5} v[\\int_{0}^{7} 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u]\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{5} v\\left[u\\right]_{0}^{7}\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =1\\int_{0}^{5} v\\left(\\left(7\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\int_{0}^{5} v\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\left[\\frac{v^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{5} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{25}{2}\\right)-(\\left(0\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(7\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{25}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{175}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["ecfa51a6-08a6-519a-a1b0-6bb584bc2c63"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "90eb973c-7cd7-5bda-8a6f-a575297ec671" :answer/id #uuid "90eb973c-7cd7-5bda-8a6f-a575297ec671" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3}}{4} - \\frac{e^{4}}{4} - \\frac{e^{7}}{4} + \\frac{e^{8}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a7aa3024-8c33-533e-ae31-5c49f1df18fc" :answer/id #uuid "a7aa3024-8c33-533e-ae31-5c49f1df18fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{3}}{4} - \\frac{e^{4}}{4} + \\frac{e^{7}}{4} + \\frac{e^{8}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0b65a186-a184-5132-a502-d8ae39b78c12" :answer/id #uuid "0b65a186-a184-5132-a502-d8ae39b78c12" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e^{8}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c0c8590b-5153-5c28-99fd-22b08634c632" :answer/id #uuid "c0c8590b-5153-5c28-99fd-22b08634c632" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{4}}{4} + \\frac{e^{8}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "983f0743-ee62-5125-95e9-f57503bfeb8c" :answer/id #uuid "983f0743-ee62-5125-95e9-f57503bfeb8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{5}}{4} - \\frac{e}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "c71fa17c-f1a9-58bd-837f-ffd76e6dc9e6" :answer-field/id #uuid "c71fa17c-f1a9-58bd-837f-ffd76e6dc9e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["90eb973c-7cd7-5bda-8a6f-a575297ec671" "a7aa3024-8c33-533e-ae31-5c49f1df18fc" "0b65a186-a184-5132-a502-d8ae39b78c12" "c0c8590b-5153-5c28-99fd-22b08634c632" "983f0743-ee62-5125-95e9-f57503bfeb8c"] :answer-field/correct "90eb973c-7cd7-5bda-8a6f-a575297ec671" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2231fad2-39e0-5330-a2a7-ac9c21f00afb" :question/id #uuid "2231fad2-39e0-5330-a2a7-ac9c21f00afb" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D e^{x^{2} + x + 4 y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):1\\le x\\le 5,\\quad 2\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le x\\le 5,\\quad 2\\le x^{2} + 4 y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x^{2} + 4 y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):1\\le u\\le 5,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\2 x & 4\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- \\frac{u^{2}}{4} + \\frac{v}{4}$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D e^{x^{2} + x + 4 y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_D e^{x+(x^{2} + 4 y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta e^{u + v}\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(e^{u + v}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int_{1}^{5} [\\int_{2}^{3} e^{u} e^{v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int_{1}^{5} \\left(e^{u}\\right)[\\int_{2}^{3} e^{v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int_{1}^{5} \\left(e^{u}\\right)\\left[e^{v}\\right]_{2}^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int_{1}^{5} \\left(e^{u}\\right)\\left(\\left(e^{3}\\right)-(\\left(e^{2}\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- e^{2} + e^{3}\\right)\\int_{1}^{5} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- e^{2} + e^{3}\\right)\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{1}^{5} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- e^{2} + e^{3}\\right)\\left(\\left(e^{5}\\right)-(\\left(e\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{5} - e\\right)\\cdot \\left(- e^{2} + e^{3}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{e^{3}}{4} - \\frac{e^{4}}{4} - \\frac{e^{7}}{4} + \\frac{e^{8}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["c71fa17c-f1a9-58bd-837f-ffd76e6dc9e6"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "d0ee4ba4-229e-5664-895e-136f3ef23945" :answer/id #uuid "d0ee4ba4-229e-5664-895e-136f3ef23945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{6}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "62e518e1-7f15-50d7-b3d9-6f2e7e0ec706" :answer/id #uuid "62e518e1-7f15-50d7-b3d9-6f2e7e0ec706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{4}}{4} + \\frac{e^{6}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "10c1298d-2a3f-5806-a08e-4abe4508710b" :answer/id #uuid "10c1298d-2a3f-5806-a08e-4abe4508710b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2 e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "b0895210-4fe6-59d4-81bd-4a7b6f99774c" :answer/id #uuid "b0895210-4fe6-59d4-81bd-4a7b6f99774c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "0d4f8852-8c2d-52c3-9bfe-2c07f2a7d249" :answer/id #uuid "0d4f8852-8c2d-52c3-9bfe-2c07f2a7d249" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{4}}{4} + \\frac{e^{6}}{4}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1c3a5904-bf08-5994-9567-c34370267b6a" :answer-field/id #uuid "1c3a5904-bf08-5994-9567-c34370267b6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["d0ee4ba4-229e-5664-895e-136f3ef23945" "62e518e1-7f15-50d7-b3d9-6f2e7e0ec706" "10c1298d-2a3f-5806-a08e-4abe4508710b" "b0895210-4fe6-59d4-81bd-4a7b6f99774c" "0d4f8852-8c2d-52c3-9bfe-2c07f2a7d249"] :answer-field/correct "62e518e1-7f15-50d7-b3d9-6f2e7e0ec706" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "2d2b5012-62ca-5818-b5dd-c30729dfd6d5" :question/id #uuid "2d2b5012-62ca-5818-b5dd-c30729dfd6d5" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D e^{2 x + 6 y} \\left(x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):2\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 2\\le x + 3 y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n2\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 2\\le x + 3 y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x + 3 y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):2\\le u\\le 3,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 3\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- \\frac{u}{3} + \\frac{v}{3}$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D e^{2 x + 6 y} \\left(x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{2}^{3} [\\int_{2}^{3} e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{2}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)[\\int_{2}^{3} e^{2 v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{2}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left[\\frac{e^{2 v}}{2}\\right]_{2}^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{2}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)-(\\left(\\frac{e^{4}}{2}\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\int_{2}^{3} u - 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{2} - u\\right]_{2}^{3} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)+\\left(-3\\right)-(\\left(2\\right)+\\left(-2\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =- \\frac{e^{4}}{4} + \\frac{e^{6}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["1c3a5904-bf08-5994-9567-c34370267b6a"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "6e820050-7944-5473-b303-2ec464e7466f" :answer/id #uuid "6e820050-7944-5473-b303-2ec464e7466f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1064" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fc7f8432-2a60-57db-9845-37922668dac4" :answer/id #uuid "fc7f8432-2a60-57db-9845-37922668dac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15071}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ce456d12-162a-5dbd-9b9e-a859e73acc05" :answer/id #uuid "ce456d12-162a-5dbd-9b9e-a859e73acc05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4435}{6}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "a6a9ff0e-0926-5538-8866-cacb621fc637" :answer/id #uuid "a6a9ff0e-0926-5538-8866-cacb621fc637" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6209}{10}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4279263b-c0d7-5a75-9245-547ed9b0ca6e" :answer/id #uuid "4279263b-c0d7-5a75-9245-547ed9b0ca6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{6209}{5}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6c4e2778-b9c5-5559-851a-c35614d178b4" :answer-field/id #uuid "6c4e2778-b9c5-5559-851a-c35614d178b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["6e820050-7944-5473-b303-2ec464e7466f" "fc7f8432-2a60-57db-9845-37922668dac4" "ce456d12-162a-5dbd-9b9e-a859e73acc05" "a6a9ff0e-0926-5538-8866-cacb621fc637" "4279263b-c0d7-5a75-9245-547ed9b0ca6e"] :answer-field/correct "a6a9ff0e-0926-5538-8866-cacb621fc637" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "c0c650a1-6d32-58bd-afa1-47278ef42758" :question/id #uuid "c0c650a1-6d32-58bd-afa1-47278ef42758" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D x y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):2\\le \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}}\\le 5,\\quad 2\\le y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n2\\le \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}}\\le 5,\\quad 2\\le y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}}\\,\\text{and}\\,v=y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):2\\le u\\le 5,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}} & \\frac{x y}{\\left(16 - y^{2}\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\\\\0 & 1\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=\\sqrt{16 - y^{2}}=\\sqrt{16 - v^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u \\sqrt{16 - v^{2}},\\ y=v$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D x y^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta u v^{2} \\sqrt{16 - v^{2}}\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(u v^{2} \\sqrt{16 - v^{2}}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\sqrt{16 - v^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta u v^2(16-v^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\int_{2}^{5} \\left(u\\right)[\\int_{2}^{3} - v^{4} + 16 v^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =1\\int_{2}^{5} \\left(u\\right)\\left[- \\frac{v^{5}}{5} + \\frac{16 v^{3}}{3}\\right]_{2}^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =1\\int_{2}^{5} \\left(u\\right)\\left(\\left(- \\frac{243}{5}\\right)+\\left(144\\right)-(\\left(- \\frac{32}{5}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{128}{3}\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{887}{15}\\right)\\int_{2}^{5} u\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{887}{15}\\right)\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{2}\\right]_{2}^{5} \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{887}{15}\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{25}{2}\\right)-(\\left(2\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(1\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{21}{2}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{887}{15}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{6209}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["6c4e2778-b9c5-5559-851a-c35614d178b4"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "7ba8c046-a1d6-57f4-892f-a3534d0ab529" :answer/id #uuid "7ba8c046-a1d6-57f4-892f-a3534d0ab529" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4 e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "92a20fe8-0398-5656-98ae-5d0e61b59958" :answer/id #uuid "92a20fe8-0398-5656-98ae-5d0e61b59958" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{2}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "4074b3cc-1ff5-5c70-89f9-b1e0666b238b" :answer/id #uuid "4074b3cc-1ff5-5c70-89f9-b1e0666b238b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{2}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "460e33d6-5dea-5a33-b627-08305e3a3d77" :answer/id #uuid "460e33d6-5dea-5a33-b627-08305e3a3d77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "7f7b56a2-872b-5d71-bb5e-f2946e4092da" :answer/id #uuid "7f7b56a2-872b-5d71-bb5e-f2946e4092da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2 e^{3}}{3} - \\frac{2 e}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "9c9ffaca-07de-5914-8dbf-895c92d16c7e" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9ffaca-07de-5914-8dbf-895c92d16c7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["7ba8c046-a1d6-57f4-892f-a3534d0ab529" "92a20fe8-0398-5656-98ae-5d0e61b59958" "4074b3cc-1ff5-5c70-89f9-b1e0666b238b" "460e33d6-5dea-5a33-b627-08305e3a3d77" "7f7b56a2-872b-5d71-bb5e-f2946e4092da"] :answer-field/correct "92a20fe8-0398-5656-98ae-5d0e61b59958" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "fad3fa36-b948-59c1-b3bc-708b975b0f34" :question/id #uuid "fad3fa36-b948-59c1-b3bc-708b975b0f34" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D e^{x^{2} + x + 3 y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):1\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le x^{2} + 3 y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 1\\le x^{2} + 3 y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x^{2} + 3 y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):1\\le u\\le 3,\\,1\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\2 x & 3\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- \\frac{u^{2}}{3} + \\frac{v}{3}$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D e^{x^{2} + x + 3 y}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_D e^{x+(x^{2} + 3 y)}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta e^{u + v}\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(e^{u + v}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} [\\int_{1}^{3} e^{u} e^{v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(e^{u}\\right)[\\int_{1}^{3} e^{v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(e^{u}\\right)\\left[e^{v}\\right]_{1}^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(e^{u}\\right)\\left(\\left(e^{3}\\right)-(\\left(e\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3} - e\\right)\\int_{1}^{3} e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3} - e\\right)\\left[e^{u}\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3} - e\\right)\\left(\\left(e^{3}\\right)-(\\left(e\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3} - e\\right)\\cdot \\left(e^{3} - e\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{e^{2}}{3} - \\frac{2 e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["9c9ffaca-07de-5914-8dbf-895c92d16c7e"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "a376fd42-0744-52dd-a934-28272c20671d" :answer/id #uuid "a376fd42-0744-52dd-a934-28272c20671d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "640d0292-c344-5d5e-9a14-b447496b8f72" :answer/id #uuid "640d0292-c344-5d5e-9a14-b447496b8f72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4 e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1090fa4f-2de9-5a71-b762-f9c4b206e1c7" :answer/id #uuid "1090fa4f-2de9-5a71-b762-f9c4b206e1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "d3e93479-2c09-5768-8f64-ed59388e0706" :answer/id #uuid "d3e93479-2c09-5768-8f64-ed59388e0706" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "- \\frac{e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f27ea39a-86a0-5aeb-ab5d-b1302b3e4a29" :answer/id #uuid "f27ea39a-86a0-5aeb-ab5d-b1302b3e4a29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ccb83526-61fd-5cdc-9d18-5c81f0f664bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "ccb83526-61fd-5cdc-9d18-5c81f0f664bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["a376fd42-0744-52dd-a934-28272c20671d" "640d0292-c344-5d5e-9a14-b447496b8f72" "1090fa4f-2de9-5a71-b762-f9c4b206e1c7" "d3e93479-2c09-5768-8f64-ed59388e0706" "f27ea39a-86a0-5aeb-ab5d-b1302b3e4a29"] :answer-field/correct "d3e93479-2c09-5768-8f64-ed59388e0706" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "261bbf3c-0c9b-595d-8e0e-d4b85f4e6d85" :question/id #uuid "261bbf3c-0c9b-595d-8e0e-d4b85f4e6d85" :question/problem "Use a change of variables to evaluate the double integral\n\n$$\n\\iint_D e^{2 x + 6 y} \\left(x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y\n$$\n\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y):1\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 2\\le x + 3 y\\le 3\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's define a transformation $T$ as follows:\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThis transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required integral, we can use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dxdy={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(x(u,v),y(u,v))\\,|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv\n$$\n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required integral, we proceed as follows:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nThe inequalities that define the region $D,$\n\n$$\n1\\le x\\le 3,\\quad 2\\le x + 3 y\\le 3,\n$$\n\nsuggest that we use the change of variables\n\n$$\nu=x\\,\\text{and}\\,v=x + 3 y.\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$\n\nOur domain in the $uv$-plane is\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(u,v):1\\le u\\le 3,\\,2\\le v\\le 3\\}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)} & =\\left|\\begin{matrix}\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial u}{\\partial y}\\\\\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial x}&\\frac{\\partial v}{\\partial y}\\end{matrix}\\right|\\\\&=\\left|\\left[\\begin{matrix}1 & 0\\\\1 & 3\\end{matrix}\\right]\\right|\\\\&=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}=\\left(\\frac{\\partial(u,v)}{\\partial(x,y)}\\right)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\ne0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$ In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\nSolving the transformation equations gives $x=u,\\ y=- \\frac{u}{3} + \\frac{v}{3}$, so the transformation is one-to-one on this domain.\n\n**Step 5**: Perform the change of variables, and evaluate the integral:\n\nPerforming the change of variables, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D e^{2 x + 6 y} \\left(x - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\,\\mathrm{d}y & =\\iint_\\Delta e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\iint_\\Delta \\left(e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\,\\mathrm{d}v \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} [\\int_{2}^{3} e^{2 v} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)[\\int_{2}^{3} e^{2 v}\\,\\mathrm{d}v]\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left[\\frac{e^{2 v}}{2}\\right]_{2}^{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int_{1}^{3} \\left(u - 1\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)-(\\left(\\frac{e^{4}}{2}\\right))\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\int_{1}^{3} u - 1\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\left[\\frac{u^{2}}{2} - u\\right]_{1}^{3} \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right)\\left(\\left(\\frac{9}{2}\\right)+\\left(-3\\right)-(\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)+\\left(-1\\right))\\right) \\\\ & =\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(2\\right)\\cdot \\left(- \\frac{e^{4}}{2} + \\frac{e^{6}}{2}\\right) \\\\ & =- \\frac{e^{4}}{3} + \\frac{e^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["ccb83526-61fd-5cdc-9d18-5c81f0f664bc"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "27afb95b-6e94-5412-95d8-8411c71548a3" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186198373.py"} [:db/add 17592186198373 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186198373 :knowledge-point/questions ["80d403dd-76fc-5ee3-bdb6-3cb3268156ab" "aed38c63-62c9-5b3d-b676-25f7dc003cd0" "4f71a0e9-4f26-53c3-82c6-851fe7d02505" "8be55c52-9e48-5369-b995-805f82de11f4" "f3bd7c92-8f56-539e-bf05-cdd21947011e" "2231fad2-39e0-5330-a2a7-ac9c21f00afb" "2d2b5012-62ca-5818-b5dd-c30729dfd6d5" "c0c650a1-6d32-58bd-afa1-47278ef42758" "fad3fa36-b948-59c1-b3bc-708b975b0f34" "261bbf3c-0c9b-595d-8e0e-d4b85f4e6d85"]} [:db/ensure 17592186198373 :knowledge-point/validate]]
